      "intent": "the same, at an address whose leaf the state holds with nonce 0, no balance, no code and two slots: the creation does not collide on storage alone, and charges and counts the address, empty under EIP-161, as a new account; the slot the constructor writes, first accessed after the creation, reads zero, so its write is a fresh slot that the destruction gives back; the slot never accessed makes no record; the leaf, present at the transaction's start, keeps its charge, its rise and its record; and the account is deleted"
